[center][size=6]BlackjackCheat[/size]
[size=3]A deck-ahead advisor for RDR2's single-player blackjack minigame[/size][/center]

[center][color=#FF8000][b]This is an advisor overlay, not an auto-play bot -- you still play every hand yourself, it just tells you the mathematically correct move before you make it.[/b][/color][/center]

[hr][/hr]
[size=4][b]What it does[/b][/size]

The single-player blackjack table (bjack_sp) deals an entire round from one fixed, already-shuffled 52-card deck. That means the dealer's face-down hole card is already real, dealt data the moment the round starts -- it's just hidden on your screen, not random. BlackjackCheat reads it directly, and then simulates the dealer's forced stand-on-17 draw-out straight off the same deck array, re-running the simulation every frame so it's exact by the time the dealer's real turn actually begins.

Because your own hand's next cards are exact, known data too (nothing else can draw from the shared deck cursor mid-turn), the hit/stand/double advice isn't a textbook basic-strategy chart guessing at an unknown next card -- it tries every legal stopping point for your hand and recommends whichever one actually beats the simulated dealer outcome. Split/no-split still comes from a standard pair chart (including correct split-Ace handling: one forced card each, no further action), and an insurance Yes/No call is shown whenever the dealer shows an Ace.

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Dealer hole card icon[/b] -- see the dealer's real hidden card the instant it's dealt.
[*][b]"Next cards" preview strip[/b] -- the exact upcoming cards your hand would draw.
[*][b]Deck-derived hit/stand/double advice[/b] -- simulated against real future cards, not a probability chart.
[*][b]Split advice[/b] -- pair chart, with correct split-Ace forced-stand behavior.
[*][b]Insurance advice[/b] -- Yes/No whenever the dealer shows an Ace.
[*][b]Zero setup[/b] -- the overlay is enabled automatically, no menu, no keybind, no configuration required to just work.
[*][b]Read-only[/b] -- no game-memory writes, no native game-state manipulation. It only reads and displays data the game has already dealt.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=http://www.dev-c.com/rdr2/scripthookrdr2/]ScriptHookRDR2[/url] matching game build [b]1491.50[/b]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install ScriptHookRDR2 per its own instructions if you haven't already.
[*]Drop [b]BlackjackCheat.asi[/b] into your RDR2 install folder (next to RDR2.exe).
[*]Launch the game, sit down at a single-player blackjack table.
[/list]
That's it -- the overlay activates automatically once you're seated with a hand dealt.

[size=4][b]Configuration[/b][/size]
A [b]BlackjackCheat.ini[/b] is created next to the .asi on first run, with three toggles under [b][General][/b]:
[list]
[*][b]ShowDealerHand[/b] -- the dealer hole-card icon
[*][b]ShowAdvice[/b] -- the hit/stand/double/split/insurance readout
[*][b]ShowDeckPrediction[/b] -- the "next cards" preview strip
[/list]
All default to [b]true[/b]; set any to [b]false[/b] to hide that part of the HUD.

[size=4][b]Compatibility / limitations[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Built against game build [b]1491.50[/b] specifically -- struct offsets are hardcoded from that build's own scripts and aren't guaranteed to hold on any other build/patch.
[*]Single-player [b]bjack_sp[/b] only -- not tested against, and not intended for, any multiplayer table.
[*]Advisor-only by design: it will never place bets, hit, stand, or otherwise act on your behalf.
[/list]

